WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:01.901
-It's great to see you.

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.469
This has been
a delightful evening

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:05.672
because you came and you watched
the debates with us.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.006
-I did.
-Which was lovely.

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:09.542
You sat in the writers room,
and it did seem like --

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.944
You obviously have done
Elizabeth Warren on the show.

00:00:11.944 --> 00:00:13.980
-I sure have.
-And it seemed like last night

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:17.417
she was maybe
inspired by your outfit.

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:18.818
-Yeah, yeah.
-There we go.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:21.520
I mean, that's on the money.
-I am a fashion icon.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.222
Gosh, she was
so happy last night.

00:00:23.222 --> 00:00:24.390
-She was very happy.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:26.225
-She looked like a girl
on her wedding day

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:29.662
when everyone who ever bullied
her was getting a divorce.

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:31.397
[ Laughter ]
She just --

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:35.668
She was in the --
"I am fighting."

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:37.136
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.136 --> 00:00:40.873
"I got a plan for my fight
and a fight for my plan.

00:00:40.873 --> 00:00:44.510
We're fighting for plans
everywhere."

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:46.979
-She does. She loves a plan.
-She loves a plan.

00:00:46.979 --> 00:00:49.081
-She loves a good plan.
-In the fight for a plan.

00:00:49.081 --> 00:00:50.416
-Yes.
-Yes.

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:53.853
-And there was someone tonight
who didn't like plans.

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:56.722
Marianne Williamson
was very anti-plan.

00:00:56.722 --> 00:00:58.958
-Gosh, I wish there was
an "SNL" show this week.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.159
-Yeah.

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:02.094
Marianne was the one
where you thought like,

00:01:02.094 --> 00:01:05.064
"Oh, she might not
make it to the fall."

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:06.765
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.765 --> 00:01:08.968
The window for Marianne
Williamson impressions

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:11.437
might be closing fast.
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:13.606
She was a shining comet.

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:15.975
Yeah, she was like -- she was --
I'll just do a --

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:18.144
-Will you do a little --
just a little taste?

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:20.146
-I was practicing
while we were watching.

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:24.717
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:27.487
"I-I've heard a lot of plans
here tonight, and if we --

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:29.722
we think plans
are gonna beat Donald Trump,

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:31.157
we got another thing coming.

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:35.862
My plan is to gather all
the sage in America and burn it.

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:38.998
My plan is to harness
the energy of babies

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:41.467
to finally put
a man on the moon.

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:44.137
And I said to
the President of New Zealand,

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:46.372
I said,
'Girlfriend, you're so on.'

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:49.642
And I would say to Donald Trump,
'Boyfriend, you chill.'

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:50.777
Thank you."

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:51.744
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:55.948
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:55.948 --> 00:01:57.483
-We got a little taste.

00:01:57.483 --> 00:02:00.753
-Oh, what a star.

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:02.588
-What a star. She is a star.

00:02:02.588 --> 00:02:04.891
It was wonderful
to have her there.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:07.693
This is a fantastic film
that you're in, "Yesterday,"

00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:09.828
and it's a fantastic premise.

00:02:09.828 --> 00:02:14.266
For those who don't know,
it's basically a gentleman --

00:02:14.266 --> 00:02:17.536
There's a power outage and when
the power comes back on,

00:02:17.536 --> 00:02:19.005
the Beatles never existed

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:21.073
and he is the only one
who knows all the songs.

00:02:21.073 --> 00:02:25.344
-Yes, and that leads him
into a situation.

00:02:25.344 --> 00:02:27.279
He tries to pass them off
as his own.

00:02:27.279 --> 00:02:29.949
But it's the best premise
I've ever heard for a movie.

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:34.286
And it's a really beautiful love
story about music and love

00:02:34.286 --> 00:02:37.657
and the Beatles and how much
poorer our culture would be

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:39.525
without the Beatles,
had they never existed.

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:41.494
-Danny Boyle. You got to
work with Danny Boyle.

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:43.462
-Danny Boyle directed.
Richard Curtis wrote it.

00:02:43.462 --> 00:02:44.997
It was the best.
-That's fantastic.

00:02:44.997 --> 00:02:47.266
Obviously, you were in London.
You were shooting in the U.K.

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:51.503
And you went and you saw --
You have ancestry there.

00:02:51.503 --> 00:02:53.406
You have lineage.
-I am of Scottish descent.

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:54.574
-Scottish descent.
Yeah, you can tell.

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:58.444
-You can tell
from the fabric of my blaze.

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.012
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.012 --> 00:03:03.182
Yeah, my great-grandfather
was born on this little island

00:03:03.182 --> 00:03:06.218
called Tiree,
which is like this,

00:03:06.218 --> 00:03:08.121
and I wanted to go,

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:11.157
and the night before I went,
I was in Glasgow,

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:13.792
buying sunblock at a pharmacy,

00:03:13.792 --> 00:03:16.896
and I said to the lady, "I'm
going to this little island.

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:18.330
My great-grandfather,"
whatever, whatever,

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:23.236
and suddenly I was transported
into a Peter Jackson movie

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:27.407
because she was like, "Ooh,
you're going to Tiree, then?"

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:28.640
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:31.577
"You must beware
the wee midges."

00:03:31.577 --> 00:03:32.745
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:36.748
And I was like,
"What is a wee midge?"

00:03:36.748 --> 00:03:38.684
Is that a ferry or...?

00:03:38.684 --> 00:03:43.089
And a wee midge is -- There's
these insects that swarm,

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:47.793
so she was like, "You must
beware or you will get swarmed.

00:03:47.793 --> 00:03:50.063
And they will steal
your magic beans."

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:51.497
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:52.599
So I was like --

00:03:52.599 --> 00:03:54.033
-Is there any way
to prevent the swarm?

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:57.402
-Yes. I was like,
"Beggar woman, what must I do

00:03:57.402 --> 00:04:00.373
to avoid the wee midges?"

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:04.276
And she was like, "You must
reach deep in your purse

00:04:04.276 --> 00:04:09.248
and you must pull out a coin and
you must buy Avon Skin So Soft."

00:04:09.248 --> 00:04:11.884
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:13.586
And then she disappeared.

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:16.755
-She was gone?
-Yeah.

00:04:16.755 --> 00:04:20.192
-Is this a real --
Am I about to actually --

00:04:20.192 --> 00:04:21.761
Is this a real photo
I'm gonna hold up?

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:23.095
-Yeah, yeah, that's it.

00:04:23.095 --> 00:04:25.197
-So you went to the island.
-I went.

00:04:25.197 --> 00:04:27.533
-And it turned out she wasn't
lying about the midges.

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:29.902
-Well, now, there were no midges
on that day

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:32.805
because it was windy, but this
is what it would have been

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:34.373
had there been the wee midges.

00:04:34.373 --> 00:04:37.810
So thank God
for Avon Skin So Soft.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:40.612
But what there was,
was sheep poop.

00:04:40.612 --> 00:04:42.515
-There was sheep poop.

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:44.517
-You know, when you go
to a duck pond

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:46.519
and can't figure out
a place to step.

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:49.155
It's worse with sheep poop
because those are bigger.

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:50.656
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.656 --> 00:04:53.225
-Did you enjoy it?
Are you glad you went to Tiree?

00:04:53.225 --> 00:04:57.530
-I'm so glad, and I'm so glad
I saw so many sheep there.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.365
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:00.833
Rocks and sheep.

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:06.571
And now I understand
my roots, and I love it.

00:05:06.571 --> 00:05:08.341
-We love you. I love you.

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:11.210
Thank you for being here
on a live show.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.779
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:12.779 --> 00:05:14.380
That's Kate McKinnon, everybody.

